Now it times out — the defeat overlay never appears even with all allies dead. Why?

In `executeAction`, after damage: `this.cb.onUpdate?.(); if (this.checkEnd()) return;`. checkEnd → alliesAlive === 0 → finish('defeat'). That should trigger...

Unless — allies were killed while phase was 'select' and the active unit is an ALLY that I killed. Then... `nextTurn` already shifted it. Sequence: I kill all allies during an ally's 'select' phase. The engine waits for player input that never comes! There's no timer — the engine sits in 'select' phase forever. The player is dead but the turn loop is stalled awaiting input.

That's actually a REAL edge-case bug in the game: if the active ally dies during its own turn (e.g., from a status tick in startOfTurn — burn/poison!), what happens? Look at startOfTurn: poison/burn applies raw damage; `if (!unit.alive) return;` — then back in nextTurn:

```js
this.startOfTurn(unit);
if (this.finished) return;
if (!unit.alive) {
  this.finishTurn(unit);
  return;
}
```

OK — the engine handles the active unit dying during its own turn (dot ticks). Good.

But what if the active ally dies from... hmm, in-game, allies can only die during their own turn via dot ticks (handled), or... reflect? No reflect mechanics. So the stall I created (killing allies mid-select-phase via console) can't happen in normal play. EXCEPT — wait, can it? `dealDamage` lifesteal heals attacker... enemies die during ally turn — checkEnd handles. Ally dies during ENEMY turn — checkEnd after executeAction → finish. Ally dies during own turn from dot — handled. So the only stall path is external manipulation. Not a real game bug.

Hmm wait, one more: `applyRawDamage` from burn/poison in startOfTurn — the check `if (!unit.alive) return` covers it, and nextTurn's `if (!unit.alive) finishTurn` too. And what if the unit dies from burn AND that was the last ally → finishTurn → checkEnd → defeat ✓.

OK so for the test, instead of killing allies during the ally's select phase, I should kill them during an ENEMY turn, or simply wait until phase === 'enemy' before killing. Simpler: kill allies AND also call the internal flow — I can't call module functions... but I CAN wait for phase 'enemy' or 'resolving'. Alternative: set allies to 1 HP but ALSO set their maxAether to 0... cleric heal still works.

Better approach: wait until `phase === 'enemy'` (enemy is acting), then kill all allies. The enemy's executeAction → checkEnd → defeat. Timing: enemy turns happen constantly; poll for phase==='enemy' then evaluate kill. Let me implement: poll page for `window.__warband.battle.phase === 'enemy'` up to 30s, then kill, then wait for overlay.

